-        "text": "The ward runs out of forms before it runs out of beds. Iona uses the clean backs of the pages to write directions to the gate. Every convoy leaves room for somebody who walks slowly. On the first morning without an order, Mara asks whether they should close the cordon. Nobody can think of a reason. The city will remember the missing by making space for whoever arrives next."
