+### Bard - Iven Cair
+
+Iven Cair spent years moving scenery for other people's performances. Newly admitted to the Bard discipline, he is learning to leave a pause long enough for someone else to answer.
+
+Resolving Phrase [Q]: Spend up to 3 cadence for three moving pulses, 0.75 seconds apart. Each deals 20 + 5 per cadence damage, slows ordinary enemies by 25%, and refreshes nearby allies' shield to 6 + 3 per cadence for 2 seconds. Shields use the strongest value and respect difficulty limits. Cooldown 12 s; duration 1.5 s; radius/range 145 px; base damage 20 HP.
+
+Cut In [E]: Strike along a narrow line toward the aim point, stopping at cover. Deal 65 damage and erase up to 8 hostile projectiles on that line. Warnings, beams, fields and already chosen attack positions are unchanged. Cooldown 15 s; duration 0.25 s; radius/range 210 px; base damage 65 HP.
+
+Ultimate Encore [X]: Spend cadence to place a six-pulse performance at your feet. One pulse each second deals 36 + 4 per cadence damage and refreshes 18 + 2 per cadence shield for nearby allies. The stage stays in place. It does not heal, revive, erase hazards or stack identical shields. Cooldown 90 s; duration 6 s; range 205 px.
+
+### Swordsman - Dara Flint
+
+Dara worked at a grinding bench before beginning sword training. She can judge an edge more easily than she can admit she has misjudged a distance.
+
+Measured Cut [Q]: Commit for 0.2 seconds on the chosen aim, then advance up to 90 units through clear ground and cut for 75 damage within 130 units. Cover blocks the movement and blade. Dodging cancels the committed cut; this grants no invulnerability. Cooldown 10 s; duration 0.2 s; radius/range 130 px; base damage 75 HP.
+
+Frontal Guard [E]: Hold the chosen frontal guard for 11 ticks, stopping at most 3 incoming projectiles at the blade. A real parry opens a 3-second counter: the next committed primary cut deals 60% more damage. Beams, fields, melee damage and existing warnings remain dangerous. Dodging cancels the guard. Cooldown 9 s; duration 0.36666666666666664 s; radius/range 30 px; base damage 0 HP.
+
+Ultimate Long Measure [X]: For 7 seconds, the next 3 committed primary cuts gain 40 reach and 35% damage. Misses and cancelled cuts spend their charge. This is an attack stance, not automatic damage, projectile reflection or invulnerability. Cooldown 85 s; duration 7 s; range 40 px.
+
+### Summoner - Joss Merrow
+
+Joss organized market deliveries before entering Summoner training. He remembers promises more easily than he remembers to leave enough time to keep them.
+
+Call Retinue [Q]: Call one Tatterhound and one Lanternwing into clear nearby space, up to four permanent companions. Existing companions keep their health. A full or blocked call spends no cooldown. Companions have real health, movement and attacks; they disappear with their owner or encounter. Cooldown 8 s; duration 0 s; radius/range 68 px; base damage 0 HP.
+
+Gather [E]: For four seconds, send the living retinue physically back to you at 40% extra movement speed. Each companion present at the cast can recover 12 base health once after arriving. No teleport, resurrection, repeated-arrival healing or invulnerability. Cooldown 12 s; duration 4 s; radius/range 45 px; base damage 0 HP.
+
+Ultimate Open Muster [X]: Call up to two temporary Wickerwards for 16 seconds and strengthen retinue damage by 25% for that interval. Bodies obey the same health, cover, orders and eight-companion owner limit. Expiration removes temporary forms without an explosion or refund. Cooldown 95 s; duration 16 s; range 540 px.
+
+### Ranger - Nela Venn
+
+Nela copied water-survey routes before beginning Ranger training. She is learning that a path drawn on paper can still fail the person who has to use it.
+
+Drawn Line [Q]: Spend one ready arrow and hold the chosen aim for 0.4 seconds, moving at 55% speed. Release a real 95-damage arrow with 2 pierce and 980 range. Dodging cancels the release without refunding the arrow or cooldown. Cover stops the arrow. Cooldown 11 s; duration 0.4 s; radius/range 980 px; base damage 95 HP.
+
+Tripline [E]: Place a finite cable through legal ground. After 0.8 seconds it can catch an actual enemy crossing, deal 45 damage and slow ordinary enemies by 40% for 3 seconds. A cable lasts 20 active seconds; at most 2 are placed initially. Bosses take damage without a root or attack cancellation. Full or blocked placements spend no cooldown. Cooldown 13 s; duration 20 s; radius/range 154 px; base damage 45 HP.
+
+Ultimate Surveyor's Circuit [X]: Prepare up to two legal fixed firing positions for 8 seconds. Within 34 units, each position empowers 3 committed primary arrows with 60% damage and 1 pierce. Spend the nearest position's charge when drawing, including cancelled shots. Moving away gives no boost; casting alone deals no damage or invulnerability. Cooldown 90 s; duration 8 s; range 34 px.
+
+### Alchemist - Perrin Moss
+
+Perrin worked in a dyehouse before entering Alchemist training. They trust a repeatable result more readily than a confident explanation, and still keep notes on the batches that went wrong.
+
+Small Batch [Q]: Reserve the selected recipe ingredients and brew for 0.4 seconds at 80% movement. Keep up to two recipe-locked vials. Dodging cancels the brew without refund. Flare costs cinder and chalk; Binding costs chalk and sap; Mending costs cinder and sap. Each costs one of both ingredients. Cooldown 4 s; duration 0.4 s; radius/range 0 px; base damage 0 HP.
+
+Cast Flask [E]: Throw the oldest prepared vial at a chosen point up to 300 units away, including close or self placement. It lands after 0.5 seconds. Flare deals 55 damage; its eight-second pool adds five 4-damage pulses, one every 1.5 seconds. Binding deals 25 and slows ordinary enemies by 40% for three seconds, with five brief slow refreshes in its eight-second pool. Mending restores 18 missing health. Cover blocks placement and splash. Your Flare can consume your Binding pool for 30 extra impact damage; Mending can consume your fire pool without extra healing, forfeiting its remaining pulses. Cooldown 6 s; duration 0.5 s; radius/range 300 px; base damage 55 HP.
+
+Ultimate Standard Batch [X]: Restore one of each combat ingredient, up to six each. For fourteen seconds your next three actual throws gain 50% potency and 25% radius. Begin with prepared vials and a ready throw to use the full batch at base cooldown. A miss spends its charge. Casting alone deals no damage and grants no invulnerability. Cooldown 95 s; duration 14 s; range 0 px.
+
 Ultimates begin ready and advance cooldown only during active combat. Intermissions and solo pause do not recharge them. The utility branch upgrades ultimate cooldown at depths 3 and 5, potency at depth 5, and a unique ultimate mechanic at its capstone. Ultimate cooldown reduction is capped at 40%; Focus Tonic affects Q/E only. Identical ally auras use the strongest magnitude and longest remaining duration rather than multiplying. Keyboard X and gamepad east face button activate the ultimate; a separate labeled touch control displays ready state and remaining cooldown.
 
